WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.656
Professionalism is observable behaviour. A patient sees it when you introduce yourself, ask permission, explain an examination and cover them again afterwards.
专业精神表现为看得见的行为：介绍自己、征求同意、说明检查内容，并在检查后重新遮盖患者身体。

00:00:10.656 --> 00:00:22.872
Integrity means recording the findings you actually obtained. If a measurement was not completed, state that and explain why, rather than filling the gap with an assumed normal result.
诚信意味着记录实际取得的结果。没有完成某项测量，就说明未完成及其原因，不能用推测的正常结果填空。

00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:35.280
Reliability includes checking equipment before a call, completing agreed tasks and noticing when the original plan is no longer safe. Courtesy without dependable clinical work is not enough.
可靠性包括出车前检查设备、完成已承诺的任务，以及发现原计划何时已不再安全。只有礼貌，没有可靠的临床工作，并不足够。

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:44.448
Competence includes asking for assistance. A professional identifies a limit before that limit exposes the patient to avoidable harm.
胜任能力也包括求助。专业人员应在自身局限造成可避免的伤害之前，识别局限并取得支持。

00:00:44.448 --> 00:00:55.512
In British Columbia, the Emergency Medical Assistants Licensing Board is the regulator. BCEHS is a service and employer; it is not another name for the Licensing Board.
在卑诗省，Emergency Medical Assistants Licensing Board，即 EMALB，是监管机构。BCEHS 是服务机构和雇主，不是 EMALB 的另一个名称。

00:00:55.512 --> 00:01:05.784
The regulation defines licence categories, authorized services and endorsements. A particular licence can also have conditions or restrictions.
法规界定执照类别、获准提供的服务及附加许可。具体个人的执照还可能附有条件或限制。

00:01:05.784 --> 00:01:20.376
Operational practice must also fit the service's authorization, available resources and your demonstrated competence. Reading a procedure or receiving a suggestion from a colleague does not establish that you are authorized to perform it.
实际执业还必须符合服务机构授权、现有资源及本人已证实的能力。读过某项操作，或同事建议去做，都不能证明你有权实施。

00:01:20.376 --> 00:01:28.824
When the limits are unclear, keep providing the safe care you can deliver and clarify through the appropriate clinical or supervisory channel.
界限不清时，继续提供自己能够安全实施的照护，同时通过适当的临床咨询或督导渠道核实。

00:01:28.824 --> 00:01:38.520
Imagine a colleague asks you to use a device that you have watched once but have never practised with. Familiarity with the name is different from safe performance.
假设同事请你使用一台设备，你只看别人用过一次，从未练习过。听过名称，与能安全实施操作，是两回事。

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:49.032
Check legal authority, service authorization, your capability and the patient's needs. These are separate checks; passing one does not answer the others.
分别检查法律权限、机构授权、自己的实际能力及患者需要。四项检查各不相同，通过其中一项并不等于其他项也成立。

00:01:49.032 --> 00:02:00.312
State the limitation plainly: I am not trained to operate this device independently. I can continue monitoring while we obtain a qualified operator or clinical advice.
直接说明局限：“我尚未接受独立操作这台设备的训练。我们取得合格操作者或临床建议期间，我可以继续监测患者。”

00:02:00.312 --> 00:02:08.544
This response offers a safe next action. It avoids both an unsupported attempt and simply withdrawing from patient care.
这种回应给出了安全的下一步，既避免无能力依据地尝试，也避免直接退出患者照护。

00:02:08.544 --> 00:02:22.080
Fatigue can slow decisions and make a simple calculation difficult. Illness, emotional distress, alcohol, other substances and prescribed medication effects can also impair safe work.
疲劳会拖慢决策，让简单计算也变得困难。疾病、情绪困扰、酒精、其他物质，以及处方药的影响，也可能损害安全工作能力。

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:32.832
Notice functional evidence: repeated missed instructions, inability to stay awake, an unsafe driving decision or a task you cannot reliably complete.
留意实际功能表现，例如反复漏听指令、无法保持清醒、不安全的驾驶决定，或不能可靠完成某项任务。

00:02:32.832 --> 00:02:47.280
Act on the immediate risk. Tell your partner and supervisor, arrange a safe handover of the task and follow the service's process. Concealing impairment to avoid inconveniencing a team transfers risk to the patient.
先处理眼前风险：告知搭档和主管，安全交接任务，并遵循机构流程。为了不给团队添麻烦而隐瞒受损状态，只是把风险转嫁给患者。

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:59.016
If the concern involves a colleague, describe the behaviour you observed rather than diagnosing its cause. Immediate protection and a factual report are more useful than an accusation.
如果担心的是同事，描述你观察到的行为，不要自行诊断原因。即时保护和客观报告，比指控更有帮助。

00:02:59.016 --> 00:03:10.176
Accountability means being answerable for your assessment, decisions, actions and omissions. It continues through treatment, documentation and the transfer of care.
问责意味着对自己的评估、决定、行动及遗漏承担解释责任。这种责任贯穿治疗、记录和照护交接。

00:03:10.176 --> 00:03:20.280
You should be able to explain what you knew at the time, what you did, why you chose it and what changed afterwards. Hindsight alone should not replace this actual sequence.
你应能说明当时知道什么、做了什么、为何这样选择，以及后来发生了什么变化。不能只用事后判断替代真实的时间顺序。

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:33.600
Documentation supports accountability when it contains observations, times, reasoning, actions and responses. It fails when it contains a polished story that hides a delay or uncertainty.
记录包含观察、时间、推理、处置和反应时，才能支持问责。如果只是修饰过的故事，掩盖了延误或不确定性，就失去了作用。

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:44.352
Professional responsibility also applies off duty. A patient story posted online can identify someone through combined details, even when the name is removed.
专业责任也适用于下班后。即使删去姓名，发布到网上的患者故事仍可能因多项细节组合而识别出本人。

00:03:44.352 --> 00:03:54.936
An error response starts with the patient, not with deciding who is at fault. Assess for harm, obtain the necessary clinical assistance and maintain continuity of care.
错误处理应从患者开始，而不是先决定谁有错。评估伤害、取得所需临床支持，并维持照护连续性。

00:03:54.936 --> 00:04:06.720
Tell the relevant people what is known, what is uncertain and what has already been done. Follow the service's disclosure and incident-reporting process rather than making promises about an outcome.
向相关人员说明已知情况、不确定之处和已采取的行动。遵循机构的告知及事件报告流程，不要承诺某种结果。

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:17.712
Record clinical facts in the patient record. Use the separate safety-reporting channel for the event investigation. An incident report does not replace the patient care report.
临床事实应写入患者记录；事件调查应使用独立的安全报告渠道。事件报告不能代替 Patient Care Report，即 PCR。

00:04:17.712 --> 00:04:28.896
A near miss also reveals a weak point. For example, two look-alike equipment labels deserve a process correction even if a final check prevented the wrong item from being used.
险些发生的错误同样能暴露薄弱环节。例如两个设备标签很相似，即使最后核对避免了用错，也仍应改进流程。

00:04:28.896 --> 00:04:39.984
Suppose a partner starts entering an unmeasured blood pressure. A useful challenge names the specific action and the patient-safety concern, then asks for a correction.
假设搭档开始填写尚未测量的血压。有效的提醒应指出具体行为及其患者安全风险，再要求纠正。

00:04:39.984 --> 00:04:51.024
If the concern is not resolved, escalate to the appropriate supervisor or clinical support. Do not let hierarchy turn an invented finding into a permanent patient record.
如果问题没有解决，应升级至适当主管或临床支持人员。不能因为职级差异，就让虚构结果成为永久患者记录。

00:04:51.024 --> 00:05:05.904
The BC Code of Ethics includes reporting incompetent, illegal or unethical conduct to appropriate authorities. The destination and urgency depend on the concern; gossip and public shaming are not reporting systems.
卑诗省职业伦理准则包含向适当主管机关报告不胜任、违法或不合伦理行为的义务。报告去向和紧迫性取决于具体问题；闲谈和公开羞辱不是报告制度。

00:05:05.904 --> 00:05:19.296
Describe observations, exact relevant words, actions taken and unresolved risks. Keep clinical records factual and use the proper personnel or regulatory process for conduct concerns.
描述观察事实、相关原话、已采取行动和尚未解决的风险。患者记录保持客观；行为问题使用适当的人事或监管流程处理。

00:05:19.296 --> 00:05:30.816
A clinical relationship contains an unequal distribution of information, authority and vulnerability. Boundaries prevent the professional from using that position to meet personal needs.
临床关系中的信息、权力和脆弱程度并不对等。专业界限能防止医护人员利用这种地位满足个人需要。

00:05:30.816 --> 00:05:42.288
Compassion means listening and responding to the patient's concern. It does not require sharing your private problems, offering personal money or becoming the patient's private contact after a call.
同理关怀是倾听并回应患者的担忧，并不要求分享自己的私事、提供私人金钱，或在出车后成为患者的私人联络人。

00:05:42.288 --> 00:05:54.624
Before physical contact, explain what you need to examine and why. Use appropriate covering and assistance. A clinically necessary examination still requires respectful communication.
身体接触前，说明要检查什么以及原因，使用适当遮盖并按需取得协助。即使检查确有临床必要，也仍需要尊重患者的沟通。

00:05:54.624 --> 00:06:04.080
Watch for thoughts such as this patient needs only me, or I should hide this favour from my team. Those are reasons to pause and seek supervision.
留意“这位患者只需要我”或“这次帮忙最好瞒着团队”等想法。这些都是应停下来寻求督导的信号。

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:15.816
A dual relationship occurs when your professional role overlaps with a personal, social or financial role. In a small community, encountering someone you know may be unavoidable.
双重关系指专业角色与私人、社交或财务角色发生重叠。在小社区中，遇到熟人可能无法避免。

00:06:15.816 --> 00:06:27.912
The overlap is a risk to manage, not proof that you must abandon urgent care. Provide necessary help, identify the conflict and arrange another appropriate clinician when feasible.
角色重叠是需要管理的风险，不代表必须放弃紧急照护。应提供必要帮助、识别利益冲突，并在可行时安排其他适当人员接手。

00:06:27.912 --> 00:06:38.592
Use the same assessment and documentation standards. Do not skip sensitive questions because you know the family, and do not tell mutual friends that the patient called for help.
使用相同的评估和记录标准。不要因为认识家属而跳过敏感问题，也不要向共同朋友透露患者曾求助。

00:06:38.592 --> 00:06:50.184
Gifts and special favours can create obligation. Follow the applicable gift policy, decline inappropriate personal benefits and seek guidance when the boundary is uncertain.
礼物和特殊照顾可能制造人情义务。应遵循适用的礼品政策，拒绝不适当的私人利益；界限不清时寻求指导。

00:06:50.184 --> 00:07:00.288
If a patient asks for your personal phone number, begin by acknowledging the underlying need. They may be frightened of being alone or unsure how to access follow-up.
患者索要私人电话号码时，先回应背后的需要。他们可能害怕独处，或不知道如何获得后续帮助。

00:07:00.288 --> 00:07:10.272
Then state the professional limit clearly and kindly. Offer a service-based option without promising that a referral will be accepted or available immediately.
随后清楚、友善地说明专业界限，提供机构渠道内的选择，但不要承诺转介一定会获接收或立即可用。

00:07:10.272 --> 00:07:20.352
Brief self-disclosure is only useful if it serves the patient's care. A conversation that asks the patient to comfort you reverses the professional relationship.
简短的自我披露只有在服务患者照护时才有意义。如果谈话变成要求患者安慰你，就颠倒了专业关系。

00:07:20.352 --> 00:07:30.480
If you feel unusually attached or responsible, discuss that reaction with an appropriate supervisor or support person while protecting patient confidentiality.
如果你感到异常依恋，或认为自己必须独自负责，应在保护患者隐私的前提下，与适当督导或支持人员讨论这种反应。

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:42.168
Autonomy asks whose decision this is and whether the person has the information and opportunity needed to decide. A recommendation should help the patient make a choice, not silence them.
尊重自主要求明确：这是谁的决定，以及对方是否具备作决定所需的信息和机会。建议应帮助患者选择，而不是压制其表达。

00:07:42.168 --> 00:07:54.240
Beneficence asks what good the proposed action could achieve. Nonmaleficence asks what harm it might cause, including harm from delay, coercion or an unnecessary intervention.
行善原则关注行动能带来什么益处；不伤害原则关注可能造成什么损害，包括延误、强迫或不必要干预带来的伤害。

00:07:54.240 --> 00:08:05.952
Justice asks whether care is fair. Clinical urgency and need can justify different priorities; wealth, social status or your personal liking of a patient cannot.
公正原则关注照护是否公平。临床紧急程度和需要可以支持不同优先顺序；财富、社会地位或你对患者的个人好恶则不能。

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:16.680
The principles may pull in different directions. Use them to expose the competing concerns, then explain a defensible action rather than merely naming a principle.
这些原则有时会相互拉扯。应借助它们明确冲突所在，再解释可辩护的行动，而不是只报出原则名称。

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:28.608
For adult consent in BC, capability is presumed unless the contrary is demonstrated. Disagreeing with your recommendation does not, by itself, show incapability.
在卑诗省的成人医疗同意框架下，除非有相反证据，否则推定成年人有决定能力。不同意你的建议，本身并不证明缺乏能力。

00:08:28.608 --> 00:08:39.936
Explain the condition, the proposed care, important risks and benefits, and reasonable alternatives. Ask the person to describe what those options could mean for their own situation.
说明病情、拟议照护、重要风险和益处，以及合理替代方案。请对方说明这些选择对自己的处境可能意味着什么。

00:08:39.936 --> 00:08:50.520
A capable adult can refuse care, including a choice with serious consequences. Family anxiety does not automatically transfer the decision to a relative.
具有相关决定能力的成年人可以拒绝照护，即使后果可能严重。家属焦虑并不会自动把决定权转交给亲属。

00:08:50.520 --> 00:09:05.832
If understanding, voluntariness or a possible emergency exception is uncertain, obtain appropriate clinical support and follow the consent pathway. This ethical discussion is not a complete refusal or mental-health algorithm.
如果对理解能力、自愿性或紧急例外的适用性存在疑问，应取得适当临床支持并遵循医疗同意流程。本段伦理讨论不是完整的拒绝照护或精神健康处置算法。

00:09:05.832 --> 00:09:17.496
Start by stating the dilemma in one sentence. For example: I recommend assessment in hospital, but the patient is declining because they fear leaving a dependent person alone.
首先用一句话说清困境，例如：“我建议到医院进一步评估，但患者担心被照护者无人照顾，因此拒绝。”

00:09:17.496 --> 00:09:26.976
Gather clinical findings and ask what matters to the patient. Separate a confirmed fact from an assumption about their motivation or capability.
收集临床结果，并询问患者最在意什么。把已确认事实，与对动机或决定能力的猜测区分开。

00:09:26.976 --> 00:09:40.752
Compare options that are genuinely available. Consider urgent treatment, further discussion, an interpreter, a support person or clinical consultation, without inventing resources you cannot arrange.
比较确实可行的选择，例如紧急治疗、继续沟通、口译、支持人员或临床咨询，不要虚构自己无法安排的资源。

00:09:40.752 --> 00:09:51.528
Choose an action within the applicable authority, explain the trade-offs and record the reasoning. Reassess if symptoms, wishes or available information change.
在适用权限内作出选择，解释权衡并记录理由。如果症状、意愿或可用信息变化，应重新评估。

00:09:51.528 --> 00:10:02.664
In this original teaching case, the patient wants the recommended assessment. The immediate obstacle is concern for a dependent relative, not a settled refusal of medical care.
在这个原创教学案例中，患者希望接受建议的进一步评估。眼前障碍是担心需要照护的亲属，而不是已经明确拒绝医疗照护。

00:10:02.664 --> 00:10:13.032
First assess clinical urgency. Then ask whether an appropriate person or established service could help with the relative, and whether the patient agrees to that contact.
先评估临床紧迫性，再询问是否有适当人员或既定服务能够帮助亲属，以及患者是否同意联系。

00:10:13.032 --> 00:10:27.144
Autonomy supports understanding the patient's priorities. Beneficence supports needed assessment. Nonmaleficence makes us consider harm from delay, and justice requires a fair response to a social barrier.
尊重自主要求理解患者的优先事项；行善支持必要评估；不伤害要求考虑延误的损害；公正要求公平回应社会障碍。

00:10:27.144 --> 00:10:40.680
A defensible plan combines clinical care with a feasible, consent-based support step. If no support is available, explain that limitation, obtain clinical advice when needed and document the patient's decision.
可辩护的计划应把临床照护与可行、获得同意的支持步骤结合。如果没有支持可用，要说明限制，按需取得临床建议，并记录患者决定。

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:52.512
Advocacy means helping a patient access appropriate care or support. Common barriers include medication access, transport, housing, language and limited social support.
患者倡导是帮助患者取得适当照护或支持。常见障碍包括取药困难、交通、住房、语言，以及社会支持不足。

00:10:52.512 --> 00:11:04.464
Ask what is preventing access instead of labelling the person noncompliant. The difference matters: an unanswered practical barrier may continue after today's symptoms improve.
应询问什么阻碍了就医或用药，而不是直接贴上“不依从”的标签。两者区别很重要：今天症状改善后，实际障碍仍可能继续存在。

00:11:04.464 --> 00:11:18.528
Offer choices, obtain the appropriate agreement and use established referral routes. Ordinary referral consent is not a universal rule for every legally required disclosure; those duties need their own pathway.
提供选择、取得适当同意，并使用既定转介渠道。普通转介的同意要求，不能概括所有依法必须披露的情形；法定报告需使用相应流程。

00:11:18.528 --> 00:11:30.168
Do not guarantee acceptance, fund care personally or take over long-term case management. Effective advocacy connects the patient to a service while keeping responsibility clear.
不要保证获接收、私人出资，或接管长期个案管理。有效倡导是在保持责任清晰的同时，把患者连接到适当服务。

00:11:30.168 --> 00:11:40.872
Limited English is a communication barrier, not evidence of incapability. Begin with immediate safety and assessment while arranging the appropriate language support.
英语有限是沟通障碍，并不是缺乏决定能力的证据。一边处理即时安全和评估，一边安排适当语言支持。

00:11:40.872 --> 00:11:52.632
Explain to relatives that you need to hear the patient's own account. Address the patient, use brief questions and allow interpretation time rather than speaking only to the interpreter.
向亲属解释，你需要听到患者本人的叙述。直接面向患者，使用简短问题并留出口译时间，不要只对着口译人员讲话。

00:11:52.632 --> 00:12:05.376
For important choices, use the service's appropriate interpreting process rather than assuming a relative's summary is complete or neutral. Ask the patient to explain key information in their own words.
对于重要决定，应使用机构适当的口译流程，不能假定亲属概括一定完整、中立。请患者用自己的话解释关键信息。

00:12:05.376 --> 00:12:16.848
Document the communication barrier, support used, relevant understanding and agreed plan. Advocacy has improved access without changing the patient's right to participate.
记录沟通障碍、所用支持、相关理解情况及商定计划。这样的倡导改善了服务可及性，同时保留患者参与的权利。

00:12:16.848 --> 00:12:26.688
Separate observation from the patient's report. Patient states is useful when the information comes from the patient rather than an independent observation.
把观察事实与患者自述区分开。信息来自患者而非独立观察时，使用“患者表示”有助于明确来源。

00:12:26.688 --> 00:12:38.352
Record the barrier, the action offered, the relevant consent and the outcome. If a referral was offered but declined, say that accurately rather than charting a completed referral.
记录障碍、提出的行动、相关同意及结果。如果只是提出转介但被拒绝，就如实写明，不能写成已经完成转介。

00:12:38.352 --> 00:12:50.544
Avoid moral labels such as difficult or uncooperative when you can describe the behaviour and context. For example, the patient declined the proposed service after its purpose was explained.
能够描述行为和背景时，避免使用“难缠”“不配合”等道德化标签。例如：“解释服务目的后，患者拒绝所建议的服务。”

00:12:50.544 --> 00:13:01.608
Use the patient record for relevant care information. A dispute with a colleague belongs in the appropriate reporting process; include any clinically relevant effect on care factually.
患者记录用于相关照护信息。与同事的争议应进入适当报告流程；如果对照护造成相关影响，则在临床记录中客观写明。

00:13:01.608 --> 00:13:10.008
Pause and form a response before reading the model reasoning. Your answer should protect information without becoming hostile to the neighbour.
请先暂停，形成自己的回应，再查看示范推理。你的回答应保护信息，同时不必对邻居表现敌意。

00:13:10.008 --> 00:13:19.824
A suitable response is: I cannot discuss someone else's health information. Thank you for offering help; please give us space to continue our work.
一种合适回应是：“我不能讨论他人的健康信息。谢谢你愿意帮忙，请给我们一些空间继续工作。”

00:13:19.824 --> 00:13:31.344
The gift and request create a boundary concern. Do not exchange information for a favour, and follow the service's gift policy. Record only what is relevant to the patient's care.
礼物与索取消息构成专业界限风险。不能用信息交换人情，并应遵守机构礼品政策。患者记录只写与照护相关的内容。

00:13:31.344 --> 00:13:42.648
Explain the principles: confidentiality protects trust; autonomy respects the patient's expressed wish; professional boundaries prevent private influence over care.
说明相应原则：保密保护信任；尊重自主支持患者已表达的意愿；专业界限防止私人利益影响照护。
